<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9962" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίθῠρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύρα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>opposite the door,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ἀντίθυρον κλισίης</span>
			<i>opposite the door</i> of the house, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				16.159
			</span></i>, as the Sch.; or it may be a neut. Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίθυρον</span>
			<i>the part facing the door, vestibule,</i> as it is in 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βᾶτε κατ᾽ ἀντιθύρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					1433
				</span></i>
			, ubi v.
			<i><span class="en">
				Herm.
			</span></i>: in <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Symp.</u>
				8
			</span></i>, <i>the side of a room facing the door,</i> cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Alex.</u>
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Dom.</u>
				26
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
